</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The documentation website has one sentence with an imprecision that has me blocked.   On the section titled &quot;How Request URI is Matched&quot;  here http://cxf.apache.org/docs/jax-rs.html#JAX-RS-UnderstandingtheBasics<br/>
<br/>
The first sentence says: &quot;Lets assume you have a web application called &#39;rest&#39; &quot;.<br/>
<br/>
QUESTION IS: Where exactly to we specify the name of the web application?   Is it the display-name in the web.xml?   Is it the artifact name in the maven pom.xml file?   Or is it something else?    The location where the name of the web-application is specified needs to be specified here to avoid any confusion! <br/>
<br/>
I simply don&#39;t know what exactly this sentence is referring to!<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
