                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently we return a Fault with a AuthenticationException when JAAS login fails.<br/>
<br/>
The proper response would be a 401 status with a suitable WWW-Authenticate header.<br/>
<br/>
I experimented with turning the AuthenticationException into a 401 response in the http transport. Not sure where to take auth type and realm from though. I am also not sure how to distinguish basic auth from WSS Security UsernameToken. As in the second case 401 is probably not correct.
  </td>
