</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-5925                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      To improve debugging of Jexl scripts it will be helpful to provide a logging util.<br/>
<br/>
You can create log statements like this:<br/>
{code}<br/>
LOG:fine(&quot;Debug message&quot;);<br/>
LOG:info(&quot;Useful information&quot;);<br/>
LOG:warning(&quot;This is a warning&quot;);<br/>
LOG:severe(&quot;Error message&quot;);<br/>
{code}<br/>
(on) Note the colon instead of the dot after LOG<br/>
<br/>
If you don&#39;t want to use the {{java.util.logging.Logger}} you can setup for example a SLF4J logger like this:<br/>
{code}<br/>
org.slf4j.Logger logger = org.slf4j.LoggerFactory.getLogger(MyMapperTest.class);<br/>
jcm = new JexlClaimsMapper();<br/>
jcm.getJexlEngine().getFunctions().put(&quot;LOG&quot;, logger);<br/>
{code}
  </td>
