                <tr id="issuerow12823769" rel="12823769" data-issuekey="CXF-6372" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6372" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6372">CXF-6372</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Generating distinct claim values for multi-value LDAP attributes
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Jan Bernhardt
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jan Bernhardt
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jan Bernhardt
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 24/Apr/15 15:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 21/Oct/16 18:46 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Apr/15 07:16 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        STS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-4543                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The LDAP claim handler generates only a single value element for a claim with delimited values, even thou a claim also supports multiple distinct values.<br/>
<br/>
This task is about to improve this behavior.<br/>
<br/>
Old behavior sample: {{memberOf}} attribute from LDAP would be generated like this in the SAML token:<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;saml2:AttributeStatement&gt;<br/>
	&lt;saml2:Attribute Name=&quot;.../05/identity/claims/role&quot; NameFormat=&quot;urn:oasis:names:tc:SAML:2.0:attrname-format:unspecified&quot;&gt;<br/>
		&lt;saml2:AttributeValue xsi:type=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;admin;user;manager&lt;/saml2:AttributeValue&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/saml2:Attribute&gt;<br/>
&lt;/saml2:AttributeStatement&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
New behavior sample: {{memberOf}} attribute from LDAP would be generated like this in the SAML token:<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;saml2:AttributeStatement&gt;<br/>
	&lt;saml2:Attribute Name=&quot;.../05/identity/claims/role&quot; NameFormat=&quot;urn:oasis:names:tc:SAML:2.0:attrname-format:unspecified&quot;&gt;<br/>
		&lt;saml2:AttributeValue xsi:type=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;admin&lt;/saml2:AttributeValue&gt;<br/>
		&lt;saml2:AttributeValue xsi:type=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;user&lt;/saml2:AttributeValue&gt;<br/>
		&lt;saml2:AttributeValue xsi:type=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;manager&lt;/saml2:AttributeValue&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/saml2:Attribute&gt;<br/>
&lt;/saml2:AttributeStatement&gt;<br/>
{code}
  </td>
