                <tr id="issuerow12834167" rel="12834167" data-issuekey="CXF-6429" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6429" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6429">CXF-6429</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Provider matching when nested generic type
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Neal Hu
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Neal Hu
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 01/Jun/15 07:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Oct/16 14:28 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 09/Jun/15 13:41 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0.3            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        3.0.6,                     3.1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-6307,                                                SYNCOPE-688                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      This is TCK case:<br/>
resource class: <br/>
JAXBElement&lt;String&gt; method(JAXBElement&lt;String&gt; jaxb){<br/>
<br/>
}<br/>
Provider 1(applicaiton provided provider): <br/>
public class Provider1  implements MessageBodyReader&lt;JAXBElement&lt;String&gt;&gt;, MessageBodyWriter&lt;JAXBElement&lt;String&gt;&gt;<br/>
Provider 2: JAXBElementProvider<br/>
@Comsumes(&quot;...&quot;)<br/>
@Produces(&quot;...&quot;)<br/>
public class Provider2  implements MessageBodyReader&lt;T&gt;, MessageBodyWriter&lt;T&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The case intends to match the pre-packaged provider, we challenged the case but spec leads rejected the challenge. They mentioned the inside generic type &lt;String&gt; should be ignored, and compare the JAXBElement then compare media type(provider2 has concrete media type). But we think according to spec 4.2.2|#4 provider1 is the nearest class of the resource java type. What&#39;s your thinking, please share with us.<br/>

  </td>
