</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      CentOS 6.6, Java <br/>
java version &quot;1.7.0_71&quot;<br/>
OpenJDK Runtime Environment (rhel-2.5.3.2.el6_6-x86_64 u71-b14)<br/>
OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (build 24.65-b04, mixed mode)<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The wadl2java tool, with the supportMultipleXmlReps option, generates the wrong @Consumes annotation values for each of the POST methods that have multiple representations.  The annotation for all of the methods contains all of the media types instead of the single media type that is appropriate for the specific method.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve tested the versions listed in the affected versions field, but it likely applies to other versions as well.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

