                                            <td class="description">      When handling this SOAP fault response:<br/>
&lt;?xml version=&#39;1.0&#39; encoding=&#39;UTF-8&#39;?&gt;&lt;soapenv:Envelope xmlns:soapenv=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot; xmlns:soapenc=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/encoding/&quot; xmlns:xsd=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema&quot; xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;&gt;&lt;soapenv:Body&gt;&lt;soapenv:Fault&gt;&lt;faultcode&gt;ServerFaultCode&lt;/faultcode&gt;&lt;faultstring/&gt;&lt;detail&gt;&lt;RuntimeFaultFault xsi:type=&quot;vim25:InvalidArgument&quot; xmlns=&quot;urn:pbm&quot; xmlns:pbm=&quot;urn:pbm&quot; xmlns:vim25=&quot;urn:vim25&quot;&gt;&lt;vim25:faultMessage&gt;&lt;vim25:key&gt;com.vmware.pbm.pbmFault.locale&lt;/vim25:key&gt;&lt;vim25:arg&gt;&lt;vim25:key&gt;summary&lt;/vim25:key&gt;&lt;vim25:value xsi:type=&quot;xsd:string&quot;&gt;Invalid or null error message(vmodl.fault.InvalidArgument) {<br/>
   faultCause = null,<br/>
   faultMessage = null,<br/>
   invalidProperty = resourceType<br/>
}&lt;/vim25:value&gt;&lt;/vim25:arg&gt;&lt;/vim25:faultMessage&gt;&lt;vim25:invalidProperty&gt;resourceType&lt;/vim25:invalidProperty&gt;&lt;/RuntimeFaultFault&gt;&lt;/detail&gt;&lt;/soapenv:Fault&gt;&lt;/soapenv:Body&gt;&lt;/soapenv:Envelope&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Fault handling fails due to an unmapped namespace error (&quot;prefix xsd is not bound to a namespace&quot;).  It appears that namespace declarations from the SOAP envelope are not propagated when unmarshalling the exception detail in ClientFaultConverter.<br/>
<br/>
The relevant stack trace is:<br/>
