                <tr id="issuerow12855503" rel="12855503" data-issuekey="CXF-6531" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6531" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6531">CXF-6531</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Exception-triggerring messages are re-delivered in endless loop
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Critical
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Christian Schneider
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Waldemar Szostak
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Waldemar Szostak
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Aug/15 09:50 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Apr/17 14:01 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 19/Apr/17 14:01 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JMS,                     Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In one-way communication (fire &amp; forget), if:<br/>
* there is an exception thrown by the user code, or <br/>
* the message is not a valid SOAP message, or <br/>
* the message&#39;s SOAP body is not a valid XML, <br/>
<br/>
the exception is not handled, but instead propagated down to the message listener causing the session to be rolled back (and thus the message to be un-acknowledged), which sort of puts the message back in the topic and makes it eligible for a re-delivery.<br/>
<br/>
Of course, the message itself is not modified, so we have a circle..<br/>
<br/>
Even though this is one-way communication, I would either expect a fault message to be generated, or the exception to be logged as error and have the message acknowledged (&#39;removed from the topic&#39;). The latter scenario at least for validation or unmarshalling exception - the exception will always be generated then (unlike the user code exceptions which may be due to temporary problems).<br/>
<br/>
In my project, I need transactions in my fire&amp;forget communication to ensure the message will be processed, despite any temporary problems, eg, with the database (=exceptions from my code). However, in situations when a client sends an invalid message to my service, I definitely do not want this message to block my service by being constantly re-delivered.<br/>
<br/>
Especially, please note that currently I have no control via my code or CXF  configuration to have such invalid XML messages simply disregarded. Either I need to turn off transactions (which I do not want to do because of my business exceptions which should cause the message to be re-delivered), or override the is-one-way property (see also JMSDestination.processExceptions):<br/>
{code}message.getExchange().setOneWay(false);{code}
  </td>
