                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The soap 1.2 spec specifically states that the fault &quot;Code&quot; must be one of the 5 values enumerated in the spec.   However, CXF uses the code set in the Fault &quot;as is&quot; without any checks.   Thus, faults can be returned that are not processable by compliant clients.  <br/>
<br/>
Note: soap 1.1 spec allows the fault code to be any qname.  This only applies to 1.2.<br/>

  </td>
