                <tr id="issuerow12896002" rel="12896002" data-issuekey="CXF-6608" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6608" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6608">CXF-6608</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                java2ws -t (target namespace) option generates invalid WSDL
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Tadayoshi Sato
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Tadayoshi Sato
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 24/Sep/15 04:58 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 31/Mar/17 19:37 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 30/Mar/17 19:58 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Tooling            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-3919                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      This command:<br/>
{code}<br/>
java2ws -wsdl -t urn:com.example:ws:1.0 com.example.ws.ExampleService<br/>
{code}<br/>
generates WSDL that contains two different namespaces for the {{tns}} ({{&quot;urn:com.example:ws:1.0&quot;}}) and the schema types ({{&quot;http://ws.example.com/&quot;}}) as follows:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;wsdl:definitions name=&quot;ExampleService&quot; targetNamespace=&quot;urn:com.example:ws:1.0&quot;<br/>
  xmlns:ns1=&quot;http://ws.example.com/&quot; xmlns:tns=&quot;urn:com.example:ws:1.0&quot; ...&gt;<br/>
  &lt;wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xs:schema xmlns=&quot;http://ws.example.com/&quot; ... targetNamespace=&quot;http://ws.example.com/&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:element name=&quot;op1&quot; type=&quot;op1&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      ...<br/>
    &lt;/xs:schema&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
  &lt;wsdl:message name=&quot;op1&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;wsdl:part name=&quot;parameters&quot; element=&quot;ns1:op1&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/wsdl:part&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/wsdl:message&gt;<br/>
  ...<br/>
  &lt;wsdl:portType name=&quot;ExampleServicePortType&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;wsdl:operation name=&quot;op1&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;wsdl:input name=&quot;op1&quot; message=&quot;ns1:op1&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/wsdl:input&gt;<br/>
      &lt;wsdl:output name=&quot;op1Response&quot; message=&quot;ns1:op1Response&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/wsdl:output&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/wsdl:operation&gt;<br/>
    ...<br/>
  &lt;/wsdl:portType&gt;<br/>
  ...<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Therefore, importing the WSDL to Eclipse shows WSDL validation errors.
  </td>
