</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Setting http-conf:client Host=&quot;xxx&quot; doesn&#39;t work.<br/>
<br/>
According to the following link this should set the HTTP Host header:<br/>
<br/>
http://cxf.apache.org/docs/client-http-transport-including-ssl-support.html#ClientHTTPTransport(includingSSLsupport)-Theclientelement<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve stepped through the code in Headers.setFromClientPolicy and it is using this to create the headers.  The outbound logging interceptor also shows this header set on the message.<br/>
<br/>
However when the request arrives at the server, the Host header is set to the actual address not the value that I specified.  I have verified this with a servlet filter and also with a debugging web proxy.<br/>
<br/>
So at some point after the logging, the Host header is being lost.  Other headers (also set via http-conf:client) do get sent correctly.
  </td>
