</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Greetings!<br/>
<br/>
First of all, this is more of a question than a bug. Here it goes.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m working on a project, where the SEI class is in Maven module A, schema classes are in module B and the SEI interface is in module C. I am trying to generate a WSDL from the SEI class.<br/>
<br/>
I have run the java2ws plugin by setting the classpath to &quot;moduleX/target/classes&quot;, but the plugin throws an error, that the classes from modules B and C cannot be loaded/found.<br/>
<br/>
Is this even supported or am I doing something wrong?
  </td>
