                <tr id="issuerow12929554" rel="12929554" data-issuekey="CXF-6743" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6743" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6743">CXF-6743</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Inconsistent versions of jax-rs specs can lead to OSGi pain
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Benson Margulies
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Benson Margulies
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Jan/16 17:57 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Oct/16 14:20 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 23/Mar/16 15:20 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        3.1.6,                     3.2.0            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        SM-2810                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      CXF&#39;s dependency tree calls for:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
 &lt;dependency&gt;<br/>
                &lt;groupId&gt;javax.ws.rs&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
                &lt;artifactId&gt;javax.ws.rs-api&lt;/artifactId&gt;	<br/>
                &lt;version&gt;2.0.1&lt;/version&gt;	<br/>
             &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
However, the Karaf features asks for a servicemix bundle that only provides version 2.0 of the spec, and indeed, there&#39;s no SM bundle for 2.0.1. So, an OSGi bundle built with CXF will be prone to try to import 2.0.1 of the package in this jar, and then fail to be able to wire it.<br/>
<br/>
If CXF really needs 2.0.1, then we need an SM bundle for 2.0.1 (and the CXF feature should reference it).<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ll link the SM jira.<br/>

  </td>
