                <tr id="issuerow12929739" rel="12929739" data-issuekey="CXF-6745" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6745" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6745">CXF-6745</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Relative Schema includes/imports in WSDL are not working (becoming absolute which is a problem behind a proxy)
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Thomas Hackel
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Thomas Hackel
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Jan/16 08:32 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 21/Oct/16 18:50 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 13/Jan/16 14:51 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the (contract first/human created) WSDL there is a relative import<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;xsd:include schemaLocation=&quot;MyTypes.xsd&quot;/&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
When accessing the Services and retrieving the related WSDL the location is being replaced by an absolute address:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;xsd:include schemaLocation=&quot;http://10.1.2.3:8080/app/mappedservice?xsd=MyTypes.xsd&quot;/&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
It should be relative like:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;xsd:include schemaLocation=&quot;app/mappedservice?xsd=MyTypes.xsd&quot;/&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
This is a problem especially behind a proxy service.<br/>
The service creator does not know the &quot;final&quot; absolute address of the WSDL/Schema.<br/>

  </td>
