                <tr id="issuerow12929941" rel="12929941" data-issuekey="CXF-6747" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6747" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6747">CXF-6747</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                XSD to Java problem with enums
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Workaround
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Dusan Slivka
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Dusan Slivka
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Jan/16 20:33 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 31/Mar/17 19:37 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 23/Mar/17 17:55 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAXB Databinding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Starting with version 3, roundtrip wsdl -&gt; Java -&gt; wsdl produces output wsdl different from wsdl on input, if there are enums used. For example, I have the folowing XSD type in source wsdl:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
  &lt;xs:simpleType name=&quot;checksumType&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xs:restriction base=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;MD5&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;SHA256&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;<br/>
  &lt;xs:complexType name=&quot;DigestType&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xs:sequence&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;digestValue&quot; type=&quot;xs:string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;digestType&quot; type=&quot;tns:checksumType&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/xs:sequence&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/xs:complexType&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
which produces (cxf-codegen-plugin:3.0.5:wsdl2java) the following Java code:<br/>
{code:java}<br/>
@XmlAccessorType(XmlAccessType.FIELD)<br/>
@XmlType(name = &quot;DigestType&quot;, propOrder = {<br/>
    &quot;digestValue&quot;,<br/>
    &quot;digestType&quot;<br/>
})public class DigestType {<br/>
    protected String digestValue;<br/>
    @XmlSchemaType(name = &quot;string&quot;)  // WHY??<br/>
    protected ChecksumType digestType;<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
And resulting wsdl for published service looks like this:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
  &lt;xs:simpleType name=&quot;checksumType&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xs:restriction base=&quot;xs:string&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;MD5&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:enumeration value=&quot;SHA256&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/xs:restriction&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/xs:simpleType&gt;<br/>
  &lt;xs:complexType name=&quot;DigestType&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xs:sequence&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;digestValue&quot; type=&quot;xs:string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;xs:element minOccurs=&quot;0&quot; name=&quot;digestType&quot; type=&quot;xs:string&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- xs:string instead of tns:checksumType --&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/xs:sequence&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/xs:complexType&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
The problem is caused by @XmlSchemaType(name = &quot;string&quot;) annotation. I think resulting wsdl should be equal to source wsdl.<br/>
See also:<br/>
[https://github.com/gf-metro/jaxb/issues/21]<br/>
[http://stackoverflow.com/questions/33346803/how-to-tell-jaxb-not-to-generate-xmlschematype-annotation]
  </td>
