                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      tomcat 7, Eclipse, Spring, JAX-WS, Maven, CXF 2.7.3
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi Community, I currently have a bug on the generation objects blocking the validation.<br/>
enumerations are generated with pattern annotation as followings:<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
@Pattern.List({<br/>
        @Pattern(regexp = &quot;Saler&quot;),<br/>
        @Pattern(regexp = &quot;direct_sale&quot;),<br/>
        @Pattern(regexp = &quot;Client&quot;)<br/>
    })<br/>
    protected String typePrescription;<br/>
{code}<br/>
exp : type_saler.xsd<br/>
<br/>
during validation, the parser interprets these annotations as mandatory in all same time.<br/>
We have to manage the types Enumeration and not string pattern with annotations.<br/>
<br/>
Thanks in advance for your return.
  </td>
