                <tr id="issuerow12983861" rel="12983861" data-issuekey="CXF-6954" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-6954" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-6954">CXF-6954</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JAXRSUtils.parseMediaTypes does not support semicolons
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ryan Diehl
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ryan Diehl
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Jun/16 17:27 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 29/Jun/16 11:05 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Jun/16 13:36 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.6            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      We have a client application sending an Accept header in the following format:  <br/>
<br/>
Accept=*/*; q=0.5; application/json<br/>
<br/>
The HTTP spec seems to allow for both comma and semicolon as separator characters in this use case.  When a client sends this request, it is not split up, and results in an unsupported media type and an HTTP 406 error.<br/>
<br/>
Fortunately in our case, we are in control of the client, so we can modify the accept header.  However, this may not always be the case for us, so I am logging this ticket in hopes of getting clarification on the expected behavior.
  </td>
