</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Until now http conduits and destinations can only be configured using the http:conduit and http:destination elements in XML or programmatically by<br/>
changing the conduit or destination of an existing client or server. <br/>
<br/>
This issue will provide features that make it easier to configure http by just adding a feature. So the client or server do not need to be changed by hand.
