                <tr id="issuerow13009057" rel="13009057" data-issuekey="CXF-7074" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-7074" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-7074">CXF-7074</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                wsdl2java generates invalid Java code when fault element is imported
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Niels Bertram
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Niels Bertram
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 01/Oct/16 16:41 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 19/Mar/17 04:09 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.1.7            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Soap Binding            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-7289                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      CXF wsdl2java tooling generates invalid Java sources when the fault element  in the fault message is imported from a copmilation eposide.<br/>
<br/>
I created a wsdl that defines a xml schema with an include from a already packaged XSD/bindings jar.<br/>
<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
  &lt;xsd:schema targetNamespace=&quot;urn:io.fares.model.example.utility&quot; xmlns=&quot;urn:io.fares.model.example.utility&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;xsd:include schemaLocation=&quot;utility/Fault.xsd&quot;/&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/xsd:schema&gt;<br/>
&lt;/wsdl:types&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
it then references an element defined in the referenced schema<br/>
<br/>
{code:xml}<br/>
&lt;wsdl:message name=&quot;GetCustomerException&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;wsdl:part name=&quot;err&quot; element=&quot;u:Fault&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;/wsdl:message&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
but when it generates code it fails to fully qualify the name of the imported and already generated XML Bean / Java class.<br/>
<br/>
{code:java}<br/>
package io.fares.examples.one.services; // &lt;---- generated into the services&#39; package<br/>
<br/>
import javax.xml.ws.WebFault;<br/>
// &lt;--- I would expect another import of io.fares.model.example.utility.Fault here<br/>
<br/>
@WebFault(name = &quot;Fault&quot;, targetNamespace = &quot;urn:io.fares.model.example.utility&quot;)<br/>
public class GetCustomerException extends RuntimeException {<br/>
    public static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;<br/>
    <br/>
    private Fault fault; // &lt;--- Fault should be fully qualified class name but its not<br/>
<br/>
    // ...<br/>
<br/>
    public Fault getFaultInfo() {<br/>
        return this.fault;<br/>
    }<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
I think the problem is somewhere around {{org.apache.cxf.tools.wsdlto.frontend.jaxws.processor.internal.ProcessorUtil.getFullClzName}} but have not been able to figure out exactly why it fails to insert the fully qualified class name into the generated exception.<br/>
<br/>
An example showing the failed copmilation can be found on [GitHub|https://github.com/fareliner/design-builder-examples/tree/master/multi-dependency/service-a]
  </td>
